Some conventions used when talking about Lojban in English, for instance on IRC or in mailing lists. At least, these are the ones that I (xalbo) usually use.

* {â€¦} is used to quote Lojban text.
* *{â€¦} is used for incorrect Lojban text. 
* ?{â€¦} is used for questionable text (either a subject of debate, or to quote without asserting correctness, for instance, asking a student what, if anything, the text would mean). 
* !{â€¦} is used for text that parses, but has a surprising or wrong meaning (one not intended).
* ~np~[â€¦]~/np~ is used to indicate words (usually terminators or {cu}) that can be included or omitted without changing the parse.
* -â€¦- is used for quoting rafsi, like -mib-, the rafsi for {mi}
* "â€¦" is used for quoting English. The *, ?, and ! modifiers can be applied if needed.
* âŸ¨â€¦âŸ© is used for quoting sequences of characters. "No, you couldn't use âŸ¨laâŸ© in a cmevla pre-Dot Side."
* â€  is used to qualify a statement, to mean "This isn't actually true, but it's close enough for the current purposes." "cmevla can onlyâ€  be used as names, but not all names are cmevla."
* â€¡ is used for "I don't know whether this is actually precisely true or not, but it's close enough for now." "You use ZOI, then anyâ€¡ Lojban word as a delimiterâ€¦" (Really? What about {bu}? What about {si}? What about {fa'o}?)